lens: one text, three ways to see it, in ed

A lens is a way to see the thing at cur (`design/studio:/a lens shows a
thing/`). ed holds the text, so ed's view shows it three ways, and Tab
turns from one to the next:

	source     the text as written, the only lens typed in
	outline    its items by their indent, as rows, or as thumbs with t,
	           as fm lays out a folder
	picture    its parts and the messages between them, as sys/picture
	           lays them out

The case, carried through: design/arch open in ed
	the bar     source  outline  picture, at the top of ed in every lens,
	            over a rule as fm's head is, the one shown lit: a press
	            on a name turns to it
	Tab         the outline: a row an item, two columns in a level, the
	            item the cursor is in lit
	j, enter    the next item, then source on its line
	Tab Tab     the picture: the pieces as boxes and the messages between
	            them; Tab once more, or a press on source, is back

Why it is ed's
  A lens of the text is a view of what ed holds, so it is ed's view's, as
  rows and thumbs are fm's view's. It reads the lines as they are, unsaved
  ones too: the outline is of what is being typed, not of the file as it
  was saved. Nothing outside ed knows which lens shows: no state file, no
  second program, and no frame needed, for ed in any pane has all three.
  ed's editor is the same but for one line: Tab is listed in its keys,
  for ? to show, and acts in the view, as ctrl-v does
  (`ed/3-mode/03-normalkeys.go:/Tab is the view's/`).

Read, never typed
  In outline and picture no key types, so none changes the text out of
  sight. A move, or a click on an item, puts ed's cursor on its line, so
  source opens where the outline was; enter, a right click or a double
  tap goes to source there; esc goes back as it was; ctrl-s saves, as in
  every mode (`ed/4-view/36-lenskey.go:/lensKey/`).

What is where
	ed's terminal view    the lens shown, the bar, the keys in a lens
	                      (`ed/4-view/32-lenses.go`)
	sys/view              outline and picture, drawn in the region under
	                      the bar, as it draws fm
	outline.Text          the items, by their indent
	sys/picture           the picture's layout

What it costs
  - the bar and its rule are two lines of every ed, in any pane: the
    bar alone under twelve lines high, as fm's head is there, and
    neither under three
  - Tab in normal is the view's, so f Tab finds no tab; in insert Tab
    types one, as before
  - in gio's window ed stays source: the bar and the region are the
    terminal view's, and the window draws ed's text itself

Given up
  - studio show, a lens of its own beside ed: what it showed of the text
    is ed's now; its diff is git diff in the shell, and its run lens
    waited on tests that write what they found
    (`design/studio:/Not built/`)
